to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=-5(1)=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -5.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-5.$ But before we conclude that $-5$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-5.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(0)^{2}-5(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492073 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492073 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158535" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492073 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492073 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=-5{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492073 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fce93d41-81b4-5cb3-80dd-626cc0b50873" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492073 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge -5{x}_{2}^{2},\\,2{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge -5{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-5{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -5{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-5({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-5(1)=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -5.$   \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-5.$ But before we conclude that $-5$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-5.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-5{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-5(1)^{2}-3(0)^{2}+2(0)^{2} \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
